-- Reset Sequences to avoid ID collisions
ALTER SEQUENCE department_department_id_seq RESTART WITH 1;
-- we start user from 2 because Admin is probably 1, or just let identity handle it if we don't specify IDs.
-- wait, we should insert WITH explicit IDs or omit IDs. 
-- It is much easier to insert WITH explicit IDs to set up FKs correctly.
-- But if we insert with explicit IDs on identity columns, Postgres requires OVERRIDING SYSTEM VALUE or we can just omit IDs and rely on mapping. 
-- However, we generate data in-memory and assign them integer IDs, then we just INSERT them. 
-- Since tables are GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY, we can insert explicit IDs and then update sequences later, or omit them if we can map them.
-- Generating explicit IDs is easier. We'll just reset sequences at the end.

